# Where this node writes. Three logging configurations, because there are three of them in the
# process by design: Cassandra binds logback inside its own ClassLoader, OpenSearch binds log4j2
# inside its, and the supervisor on the system classpath has only slf4j-simple.
#
# system.log, debug.log       Cassandra, via conf/logback.xml
#                             (rolled to system.log.<date>.<n>.zip, debug.log.<date>.<n>.zip)
# audit/audit.log             Cassandra's audit log, when it is enabled in conf/cassandra.yaml
# opensearch.log              OpenSearch, via conf/log4j2.properties
#                             (rolled to opensearch-<date>-<n>.log.gz)
# cassandra-opensearch.log    the supervisor's own output, written by bin/cassandra-opensearch
#                             when the node is started with -d. A foreground start writes the
#                             same stream to the terminal instead.
